[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:Always Young]
[00:01.20]Why doesn't Aunt Jennifer tell anyone how old she is? | 珍妮弗姨妈为什么不告诉任何人她多大了？
[00:16.43]My aunt Jennifer is an actress. | 我的珍妮弗姨妈是个演员。
[00:20.47]She must be at least thirty-five years old. | 她肯定至少35岁了。
[00:24.98]In spite of this, she often appears on the stage as a young girl. | 尽管如此，她还是经常在舞台上扮演一个年轻姑娘。
[00:31.02]Jennifer will have to take part in a new play soon. | 珍妮弗很快就要参加一个新剧的演出了。
[00:35.74]This time, she will be a girl of seventeen. | 这次，她将扮演一个17岁的姑娘。
[00:40.41]In the play, she must appear in a bright red dress and long black stockings. | 在剧中，她必须穿一件鲜红的连衣裙和一双长长的黑丝袜。
[00:48.76]Last year in another play, | 去年在另一个剧中，
[00:51.52]she had to wear short socks and a bright, orange-coloured dress. | 她不得不穿短袜和一件鲜艳的橙色连衣裙。
[00:57.80]If anyone ever asks her how old she is, | 如果有人问起她多大了，
[01:02.38]she always answers, 'Darling, it must be terrible to be grown up!' | 她总是回答说：“亲爱的，长大成人真是太可怕了！”